[h1]About[/h1]
Latinised English is a localisation mod for Imperator: Rome that overrides selected vanilla Germanic-origin words and phrases with Latin-origin alternatives.

[h1]Capabilities[/h1]
[list]
[*]Replaces vanilla English strings with latinisable equivalents, including British spellings, wider Latin-ancestry vocabulary, and context-sensitive word substitutions.
[*]Preserves every engine construct inside a value, including hover commands, variables, text icons, colour codes, and literal newlines, so tooltips continue to resolve.
[*]Ships only records that differ from vanilla, keeping the override set minimal and reviewable.
[*]Mirrors the vanilla localisation tree, so each override sits at the identical relative path with the _latinised marker inserted before the language suffix.
[/list]

[h1]Installation[/h1]
    [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3843565947][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hmlendea/readme-assets/master/badges/stores/steam-workshop.png[/img][/url] [url=https://steamcommunity.com:/linkfilter/?url=https://nexusmods.com/imperatorrome/mods/35][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hmlendea/readme-assets/master/badges/stores/nexus.png[/img][/url] [url=https://steamcommunity.com:/linkfilter/?url=https://github.com/hmlendea/imperator-latinised-english/releases][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/hmlendea/readme-assets/master/badges/stores/github.png[/img][/url]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
This mod is compatible with Imperator: Rome 2.0.* on all operating systems.

The subsequent languages are currently supported:
[list]
[*]English (en): Partial (In progress)
[/list]

[h2]Load Order[/h2]
This mod targets the vanilla English localisation tree. Other mods that override the same keys win or lose according to launcher load order, so place this mod after any localisation mod it should supersede.

[h1]Contributing[/h1]
See the [url=https://steamcommunity.com:/linkfilter/?url=https://github.com/hmlendea/imperator-latinised-english/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md]Contributing Guidelines[/url] for details on how to report issues, suggest enhancements, and submit changes.

[h1]Related Mods[/h1]
[list]
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1745923673]Dracones Invictus[/url]: Expands the Dacian culture group with additional male and female names and revises the English text of the Zamolxian faith and the Zamolxis treasure.
[*][url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3513150774]Imperator: Rome – RTW-Style Loading Screens[/url]: Replaces the vanilla loading screens with artwork matching the art style of Rome: Total War (2004).
[/list]

